# Local data — never commit real campaign data outside fixtures
data/
*.csv
!tests/fixtures/*.csv
# The social benchmarks table drives the Benchmarks page and must travel with
# the repo so the CI refresh (and a fresh clone) can render it. Internal data,
# same sensitivity as config/campaigns.yaml — keep the repo private.
!config/social_benchmarks.csv
# The live benchmark dataset (Campaign Data + Platform Benchmarks, imported from
# the FOS Social Benchmarks workbook). Same reasoning as above — must travel with
# the repo so the CI refresh can compute the live Benchmarks dashboard.
!config/benchmarks_campaigns.csv
!config/benchmarks_platforms.csv
# Paid-social benchmark dataset (BrandX + Dark Posts + In-Feed/Boosted, with
# CPM/CTR/VCR). Same reasoning — travels with the repo for the CI refresh.
!config/benchmarks_paid_brandx.csv
!config/benchmarks_paid_dist.csv
